  "description": "Arkcon welcomes you to our recently renovated studio apartment to let on the ever popular Mountjoy Square East. Please email your enquiry. Phone call enquiries are not accepted due to high volume demand. We aim to respond to all enquiries, however this may not be possible. Thank you for your understanding.\n\nArkcon is thrilled to present this newly refurbished, ground floor studio apartment ideally situated on Mountjoy Square East. Set within a period building, the apartment offers convenient ground floor access with no stairs to contend with. Upon entry, you are welcomed to a modern space, with renovations having taken place in recent years. The kitchen has been fitted with modern appliances, including a four ring hob, oven, grill and more. Facing the kitchen is a table and chairs for dining and living purposes. There is a [double] bed and adequate storage space. The bathroom is gleaming and benefits from [an electric shower, providing instant hot water]. There is electric heating throughout, with electricity supplied via a convenient top-up meter. Permit parking is available on street.\n\nMountjoy Square is one of Dublin's finest Georgian squares, with its tree-lined central park offering a peaceful green space right on the doorstep. Located in Dublin 1, the square is just a short stroll from O'Connell Street, Parnell Street, Henry Street and Moore Street, placing an abundance of shops, cafés, restaurants and pubs within easy reach. Croke Park, the Hugh Lane Gallery, the Garden of Remembrance and the Gate Theatre are all within walking distance. The location is very well serviced by public transport, with Connolly Station, Busáras and both LUAS lines a short walk away, along with an array of Dublin Bus routes. The IFSC and the north docklands are within a 10 to 15 minute walk, and Dublin Airport is easily accessible via the Port Tunnel.\n\nPlease email your enquiry to make this property your own. References and documents are required by all applicants. Available now. WiFi and bins collection are included in the monthly rent. Electricity is paid via a top-up meter.\n\nThank you.",
